description:
Get a single annotation (chart note) by its id. Pass annotationId (the UUID returned by add_annotation or list_annotations). Returns the date (Y-m-d), note text, description, category, linked task_id, author email, the property it belongs to (null for global/official notes), its URL scope (context, urls, urls_used, filters) and its keyword scope (keyword_context: all or list_of_keywords; keywords: the GSC queries a list_of_keywords note is restricted to). Set includeImpact=true to also compute the before/after GSC impact around the annotation date at 7/14/30-day windows (clicks, impressions, ctr, position — each with value_before, value_after, diff, change_pct), scope-aware (the note's urls, and only its keywords for a list_of_keywords note); costs 3 credits, and incomplete windows are flagged complete=false. For a pattern-scoped note (contains / starts-with / ends-with / regex) the top-level urls and urls_used stay empty — the URLs the numbers were computed over are only in the impact block (includeImpact=true): impact.urls_used is the 30-day window's top 100 URLs by clicks (urls_used_truncated when more matched) and each window carries windows[i].urls_used for its own date range; if resolving fails, urls_used is null with urls_used_unavailable and the numbers still stand. For a note with only literal URLs impact.urls_used lists those. Use list_annotations to find an id.

Cost: free.

Examples:
```json
// Fetch one annotation by the UUID from list_annotations.
{"annotationId":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001"}

// Fetch an annotation with its 7/14/30-day before/after GSC impact inline.
{"annotationId":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001","includeImpact":true}
```
